{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"73651a459f29dd7450c6c7cc39df246c43793a49"},"timestamp":1533823481,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQxMTc2OTI5Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2755#issuecomment-411769292"},"message":"[GitMate.io](https://gitmate.io) thinks possibly related issues are https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/299 (__repr__ for *Repo classes (and others)), https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2488 (Even with #2417 cooked *Repo.add() still cannot become generators), https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2546 (We need a cross-platform convention for paths), https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1323 (get_subdatasets  should become a generator), and https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1200 (Better exception(s) for paths outside of a repo).","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"6d482d5a11a34740eb1202233c7aa984d1782d22"},"timestamp":1533823608,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQxMTc3MDA0MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2755#issuecomment-411770040"},"message":"I recently (yesterday) learned `set_metadata()` is a generator while writing datalad/datalad-crawler#13. As an external developer, I don't think having an `_` convention would have helped since I wouldn't have known the convention. A clear statement in the doc block (rather than having to trace through the code to find a yield statement) would have been more useful for me.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1533829423,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQxMTgwMzMwOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2755#issuecomment-411803308"},"message":"\u003e A clear statement in the doc block (rather than having to trace through the code to find a yield statement) would have been more useful for me.\n\nIsn't this already the case?\n\nhttps://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/d0d332c9b5e17cd6b97841697d188aacd55f870c/datalad/support/annexrepo.py#L3232-L3235","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1533829605,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQxMTgwNDM0Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2755#issuecomment-411804346"},"message":"\u003e However, the Q is, whether we should use this as a common convention to ease use even for methods that are only available as generators now (e.g. set_metadata()).\n\nI vote no.  Like @driusan, I'm satisfied as long as its mentioned in the docstring.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1533830006,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQxMTgwNjIwNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2755#issuecomment-411806205"},"message":"Let me clarify: Yes, it should be in the docstring (like in the example above). However, I was more thinking along the lines of (always) providing a companion function that works like a generate (with `_` suffix), but keep the non-generator that we already have in general.","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1533830006,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDExNzgwODMzNg=="},"target":"cd851de3146332a4116729df2a52d48e1b9de4c0d677b3a6626d968ccea978dc","message":"Let me clarify: Yes, it should be in the docstring (like in the example above). However, I was more thinking along the lines of (always) providing a companion function that works like a generator (with `_` suffix), but keep the non-generator that we already have in general.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1533830907,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQxMTgxMTQzOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2755#issuecomment-411811438"},"message":"I'm fine with the `method{,_}`  pairing for cases where a non-generator function `method` already exists.  That seems preferable to the pain or churn of a wholesale conversion of `method`.","files":null}]}